cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Jobwatch: a VS Code extension showing Hugging Face Jobs and their estimated cost in the status bar"
message: >-
  If you use or build on this software, please cite it.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Organokov
    given-names: Mukharbek
    email: mukharbek.organokov@gmail.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3093-3456"
repository-code: "https://github.com/kabartay/jobwatch"
abstract: >-
  A Visual Studio Code extension that watches Hugging Face Jobs from the status
  bar: which jobs are queued or running, their estimated cost so far, and this
  month's estimated spend. It notifies once when a job fails (naming an
  out-of-memory kill as such), completes, nears its own time limit or waits too
  long for hardware, and when spend passes a monthly budget. Cost is estimated
  from running time and the provider's own per-minute price list. Because the
  provider records no end time for a cancelled job, the extension substitutes the
  last time it observed the job running, and bounds jobs it never observed by
  their time limits rather than guessing. Read-only, with no runtime
  dependencies and no telemetry. Unofficial; not affiliated with Hugging Face.
keywords:
  - Hugging Face
  - GPU jobs
  - cost monitoring
  - Visual Studio Code extension
  - machine learning operations
license: MIT
version: 0.1.1
date-released: "2026-10-09"
